Short:        Native word processor for DOCX, ODT and Amiga documents
Uploader:     (fill in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         text/edit
Version:      1.0.2
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenWrite 1.0.2 is a native word processor for AmigaOS 3.2.

It opens and saves DOCX and ODT documents with text and common formatting,
simple tables, inline pictures, headers, footers and page setup. It exports
searchable PDF and prints through standard printer.device, so configured
OpenAmigaPrint/OpenPrint output works as a normal printer backend.

The editor includes selection, undo/redo, character and paragraph formatting,
lists, tables, embedded images, clipboard cut/copy/paste, find/replace,
automatic pagination, page setup, multi-page navigation, spelling, recovery
autosave and an ARexx port.

OpenWrite also opens ProWrite, Final Writer/Final Copy-family SWRT documents,
Wordworth, IFF FTXT, ANSI text and plain text. Unsupported or approximated
features are named in the import report.

C:OWConvert converts supported document formats from Shell scripts and runs
on any 68000.

OpenWrite needs AmigaOS 3.2 and a 68020 or better. No FPU is required.
Small documents are intended to remain usable with about 8 MB Fast RAM;
16-32 MB is the comfortable target for ordinary work.

The bundled English spelling dictionary is derived from SCOWL/Aspell data;
its licence notice is included in licenses/.

